WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.240
Watching American Horror Story is scary enough…
but how does the cast feel as they bring these

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:06.200
stories to life?

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:11.360
AHS seems to make a permanent impact on its
stars - sometimes for the better, and sometimes

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:12.000
for the worse.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:14.700
Here's how the show has changed these actors'
lives.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.300
In the early years, Evan Peters was basically
the face of American Horror Story.

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:23.539
He started out playing Tate Langdon in the
first season, and went on to star in seven

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:26.180
more seasons of the creeped-out anthology
show.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:30.100
It seemed like Peters would always be in the
cast - but that didn't turn out to be the

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:30.600
case.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:36.300
In 2019, Peters shocked fans with the announcement
that he wouldn't be returning for 1984, the

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.020
ninth season of AHS.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:40.300
"I'm making hard choices…

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:42.100
every day."

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.940
Honestly, he probably didn't miss out on much.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:47.320
"I just needed to get each of you alone with
me."

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:47.900
"Why?"

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:53.760
"So I can kill you!"

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:59.739
Prior to Peters' announcement, the actor revealed
that AHS was taking a toll on his mental health,

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:01.420
telling GQ in 2018:

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:03.399
"I don't like to yell and scream.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:04.560
I actually hate it.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:09.240
I think it's disgusting and really awful [...] Horror
Story sort of demanded that of me."

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:10.740
He went on to explain:

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:12.440
"It's just exhausting.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:16.900
It's really mentally draining, and you don't
want to go to those places ever in your life.

00:01:17.189 --> 00:01:21.020
And so you have to go there for the scenes,
and it ends up integrating it somehow into

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:21.540
your life."

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:27.119
Jessica Lange began her stint on American
Horror Story in season one, portraying Constance

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.780
Langdon, Tate's malignant mother.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:33.790
The role ushered in a whole new phase of Lange's
career, winning her a second Primetime Emmy.

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:38.750
She stuck with AHS for three more seasons,
eventually returning for Apocalypse to reprise

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:40.040
her role as Constance.

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.560
Honestly, no one plays an intimidating matriarch
quite like her.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:52.160
"Bundy, Dahmer… they started with small
animals too… until they graduated."

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:56.640
Before getting that career-changing phone
call from Ryan Murphy, Lange was going through

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:57.800
a difficult breakup.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:02.539
She had just ended a 30-year relationship
with actor and playwright Sam Shepard, and

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:04.460
had no idea what she'd do next.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:06.780
In 2019, she told GoldDerby:

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:11.291
"Going into that series somehow revitalized
me and made me understand that there was a

00:02:11.291 --> 00:02:15.200
whole way of working that I had never done
before [...]. It forced me to work in a way

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.020
with complete and total abandon."

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:18.600
The story checks out:

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:20.280
"What is this?

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:21.820
Knotty pine!"

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:25.240
Emma Roberts was tired of being typecast.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:29.080
She felt like casting directors only saw her
as a "girl next door" type.

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:33.560
So when Ryan Murphy offered her the role of
powerful witch Madison Montgomery, she leapt

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:34.560
at the chance.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.200
"Azazel, we submit to you, body and soul!

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:42.400
The lord of the underworld, we offer you our
obedience and everlasting devotion!"

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:45.580
Playing Madison clearly gave Roberts a new
sense of confidence.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:46.620
As she told Collider,

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:49.520
"It’s definitely made me a more fearless
actress.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:52.560
Things I would normally say no to, I’m more
like, 'Bring it on!'"

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:56.310
Her stint on AHS has certainly opened doors
for her, too.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:58.640
In another interview with Collider, she noted,

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:03.209
"I remember before Madison, I would go up
for parts and they'd be like, 'She's too sweet,'

00:03:03.209 --> 00:03:04.440
or 'She's too nice.'

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.820
Now, after Madison [...] no one says that."

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:08.560
It's easy to see why.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:14.780
"I mean, why wait for some phony, happily-ever-after
when you can have your piece now, I say.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:16.160
What about you Luke?"

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:21.819
Lady Gaga always wanted to break into acting
- long before her music career ever took off.

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:25.320
For proof, look no further than her bit role
on this Sopranos episode.

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:30.080
She put those acting ambitions on the backburner
for a long time - but Ryan Murphy ultimately

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:32.239
helped turn that dream into a reality.

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:35.980
He cast her as the vampiric Countess in American
Horror Story: Hotel.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.460
"I lived in New York many years ago.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:43.600
I loved roaming the streets, devouring the
pulse of the city.

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:44.600
Electrifying."

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:47.300
As Murphy told Billboard in 2015:

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:49.520
"She has always wanted to be an actress.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:53.460
She studied it in college, but she was too
terrified to go on auditions."

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:58.739
When Murphy showed her footage of one of her
scenes in AHS, Gaga reportedly began to sob.

00:03:58.740 --> 00:03:59.880
Murphy told Billboard:

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:04.560
"I was worried, but she told me later that
it was because she was so happy that somebody

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:05.460
had believed in her."

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:09.520
Gaga's newfound confidence as an actress changed
her entire career.

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:15.099
She went on to star as Ally alongside Bradley
Cooper in the 2018 remake of A Star is Born,

00:04:15.099 --> 00:04:19.650
which was nominated for several Academy Awards
and won Best Original Song for "Shallow."

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:24.660
American Horror Story: Freak Show wouldn't
have been complete without Twisty the Clown.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:29.020
The terrifying character was played by actor
John Carroll Lynch, and it was his first time

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:30.460
ever working on the show.

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:33.740
The character had a rather nasty habit of
sneaking up on innocent people and killing

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:34.240
them.

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:38.360
And the fact that Twisty barely spoke a word
made him all the more frightening.

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:42.280
That proved to be quite an actorly challenge
for Lynch, who had to rely solely on body

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:43.700
language for the performance.

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:45.620
As he told Collider in 2014:

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:49.600
"There are a lot of things that I've never
tried before because the character is silent.

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:53.060
[...] There was the challenge of being told,
'There’s almost no dialogue and we’re

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:54.600
gonna take away half of your face.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:56.800
Let’s see if you can act in those circumstances.'”

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:01.460
Judging by his nightmare-inducing performance
as Twisty, we'd say he nailed it - and became

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:03.460
a more versatile actor in the process.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:08.180
In 2018, Cody Fern joined American Horror
Story for Apocalypse.

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:11.970
He memorably played Michael Langdon, otherwise
known as The Antichrist.

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:15.930
To prepare for the part - and get into the
mindset of a ghoulish entity like Michael

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:20.480
- Fern spent lots of time reading up on theology,
psychology, and philosophy.

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:25.360
Michael has been Fern's biggest role to date,
and apparently, Fern still hasn't entirely

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:26.840
moved on from the character.

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:29.360
In June 2019, he told GoldDerby:

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:33.760
People have more [of] an interest in the darker
aspects of life.And I think it’s very much

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:36.460
about trying to understand the darkness within
ourselves."

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:38.220
"I'm a serious actor."

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:39.140
"Heh heh."

